WEBVTT

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.580
I'm Kaidou Haru.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.620
<i>I had a nostalgic dream.</i>

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.340
<i>On that day seven years ago,</i>

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.340
<i>after I'd been adopted by Haruko 
from a Canadian orphanage,</i>

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:38.350
<i>I met Haru, who was visiting 
from Japan, for the first time.</i>

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.350
<i>He taught me everything.</i>

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:49.320
<i>Happy things and not-so-happy things.</i>

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.410
Ren?

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.220
I'm going for a run.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.030
You never get tired of that, do you?

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.440
Watch out for cars.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.340
All right.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.530
<i>Then I came to Japan.</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.050
<i>It's been three months since 
I started living with Haru,</i>

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:13.690
<i>Aki, and Shima as one of their brothers.</i>

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.010
<i>Then Haruko suddenly came to Japan.</i>

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.810
I'm taking you back to Switzerland with me.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.520
What?!

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.060
You got a problem with that?

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.060
What are you talking about, 
you rotten old ha—

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.560
The rest omitted.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.990
<i>If Haru wants me to, I'll stay with him forever.</i>

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:41.230
<i>Or so I thought, but...</i>

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:15.510
Mikiko?

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.470
Oh, Ren. Good timing.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.050
If you're heading home, I'll give you a ride.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:21.880
Were you doing work for the director?

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.970
Yeah. We were talking about you, too.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:25.630
Me?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.520
Your final exams are coming up, right?

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.010
We were discussing whether you'll 
take the same exam as everyone else

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.240
or if we'll create different questions for you.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.570
I don't mind taking the 
same exam as everyone else.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.820
What are you talking about? That essay...

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.700
I discussed it with Haruko,

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.830
but Japan only offers standardized education.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.270
Since you're exceptional at everything else,

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:58.640
it's such a waste for you to struggle with 
just your Japanese language classes.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.670
But it's also necessary, 
since I'm living in Japan.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.680
You have no intention 
of going to Switzerland?

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:05.530
No.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.590
Then let me rephrase.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.780
You have no intention of living 
with Haruko in Switzerland?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:14.990
With Haruko?

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:15.940
That's right.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.930
But Haruko said CERN has been asking her

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:22.700
to return to the organization for a while.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.950
But she couldn't go because of me.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.490
Because I said I wanted to go 
to Japan and live with Haru,

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.330
she finally decided to go.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:36.500
She should've gone where 
she was needed sooner.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.720
It's my fault she was delayed.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.990
But didn't you need Haruko, too?

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:49.070
Yeah, but she could've sent 
me back to the orphanage.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.350
Oh, please. She'd never do that.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.920
Haruko is lonely.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:55.520
Huh?

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.550
It's funny, right?

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:03.360
That square came rushing 
to Japan over a single e-mail.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.650
I thought something had happened.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:12.710
But after letting her sons go twice, 
she finally realized something.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:20.130
That she was letting go of something 
important to her, and it left her lonely.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.630
What happened, Haru?!

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.020
What's wrong with your face?!

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.840
Your face is your only lifeline.
Be careful with it.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.300
What do you mean by "only"?

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:33.600
It's your only one.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:34.860
You guys!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.600
Oh, Haru-chan.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.100
Look at your face. Did you 
fight with your brothers?

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.110
Sort of.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:44.110
This is my niece. You should talk to her mom.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:46.090
Huh?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:50.420
I've always thought this place 
lacked a female presence.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:54.070
And she says she doesn't mind 
at all that you used to be a host.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:54.860
Huh?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.870
I'll bring her with me next time.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.710
Uh, Ohtomo-san...

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.640
Did you hear that? How rude.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.460
What does she mean by 
"this place lacks a female presence"?

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.760
Actually, I think she was spot on.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.390
What are you talking about?!

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:12.810
<i>Um, this is one of those things, isn't it?</i>

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.570
Haru, I'm back. Where's Haruko?

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:16.890
W-Welcome home.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.890
Haruko-san's working in the house.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.090
Ren, let's have a snack together.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.210
Today's snack is savory carrot cake.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.900
Iku, hold down the fort.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.640
He's awfully quiet for a small dog.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.160
He hasn't barked a single time.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.940
Tanuki? Now that you mention it, you're right.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.170
I've never heard him bark, either.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.260
His previous owner was an elderly man,

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.420
but Ren's taking care of him right now.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.740
Hmm...

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:57.540
I had a hard time tearing 
him away from my dogs, too.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:02.060
I don't think it'll be easy this time, either.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.790
Are you unhappy about me taking Ren away?

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.270
If Ren makes his own decision to go,
then I won't stop him.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.270
Ren must be back.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:19.080
Come on, Tanuki. Ren's 
probably with our brother.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:23.440
It's good.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.890
I'm glad. If you like something,
our customers usually love it, too.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.970
I'll try recommending it to our 
regulars who come before lunch.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.850
<i>Sometimes, I realize he's an adult 
with really clean features.</i>

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.480
<i>I only ever see him laughing like an idiot.</i>

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:43.730
Ow.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:46.820
Are you okay?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.490
Ren, if you're home, 
could you take Tanuki for—

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.310
Is everything okay?

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.170
Actually, Haru was just 
projecting a wicked aura.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.630
I'm hungry. Feed me.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:16.680
Aki, if you're going to come 
here every day to eat,

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.140
you might as well come home.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:22.120
No way. Your mom's staying 
here for a while, right?

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.390
I don't want to see her. I want beef.

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:27.270
I don't like it, either!

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:31.260
Huh? What? Why is he in such a bad mood?

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:36.160
Because lately their mother has been 
keeping Ren Ren all to herself.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.360
It's stressing him out.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.160
Iku!

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.440
No breaks for you today.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:47.500
You're so mean!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.040
Hey! Get to work!

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.760
It's what you get for blabbing 
about my private life.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:57.590
Shima told me your mom wants to take 
Ren back to Switzerland with her.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:08:59.200
You're not gonna let her take him, are you?

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.010
No.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.020
Then why are you in such a bad mood?

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.050
If I'm the only one who feels that way, 
it makes no difference.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.800
Did Ren tell you he wants to go?

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:13.050
He didn't. In fact, he told me 
he's not going to Switzerland.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.650
Then why is this happening?

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:19.020
He did say he's not going, 
but he's been acting suspicious lately!

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.900
They're always chatting away 
together and ignoring me!

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.860
God, you're so annoying!

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.410
This is why I hate listening to you complain!

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:24.320
What do you think of that?

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.920
Are you even serious about that?

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.150
About what?

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:33.420
Do you really think Ren might 
choose her instead of you?

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:37.020
Ren and Haruko-san are more 
like a family than we are.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:38.380
Are you stupid?

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.430
Who are you calling stupid?

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:42.050
Shut up! Anyway, food!

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:45.570
<i>Anyone would feel bad 
for Ren in this situation...</i>

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:00.070
<i>I think I once felt this way a long time ago.</i>

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:07.860
Haru, I was just talking with Haruko.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:11.710
We think Tanuki is less like a Pomeranian 
and more like a Spitz Mittel.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.190
Ren, I'm sorry.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.720
I need to get dinner ready.

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.460
We'll talk after dinner.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:20.820
Okay.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:26.400
That kind of half-baked attitude 
is most comfortable for Haru.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:27.980
Haruko?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.510
Since you like Haru the most,
he must love you back.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:35.450
Because you're at his side 
and never leave his territory,

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:39.240
he's subconsciously testing your love.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:42.570
He's taking advantage of your love for him.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:47.750
As long as you stay with him, 
nothing will change between you.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:51.250
Haruko, you knew?

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.860
You're such a dummy.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:58.150
You hate people, but you're living 
in a city as crowded as Tokyo.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.800
Without a single complaint, and with Haru.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.540
And then you sent me that e-mail.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:05.760
Did you think I wouldn't figure it out?

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:10.840
But... I didn't think this would happen to me.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:14.270
I didn't even think I'd be 
able to live with Haru.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:18.420
I was supposed to be 
satisfied with coming to Japan,

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.870
seeing him once, 
and telling him how I felt.

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:22.860
Unbelievable.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:27.660
When you ran back to Canada alone, 
I didn't know what to do.

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:30.150
Sorry for making you worry.

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.290
I didn't think Haru would come after me.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:39.310
With Aki and Shima to take care of, 
I thought he'd go back to Japan right away.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.550
Besides, you weren't there anymore.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:45.050
But you returned to Japan with Haru

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:47.640
just so you could grant his wish.

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:50.570
<i>She's right.</i>

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.900
Someday I want to live with all my brothers.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.860
<i>That was supposed to satisfy me.</i>

00:11:58.460 --> 00:11:59.270
<i>But...</i>

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:03.320
Haru, sorry. Haruko found out.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:04.820
F-Found out?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:08.320
M-Mom did?

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.330
How I feel about you...

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:13.580
Huh? Oh, your feelings?

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:16.840
That you love me? That's all?

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:18.840
Don't say it like that!

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:22.760
What? But anyone could 
tell that by looking at you.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:23.620
Huh?

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.140
Forget it.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:32.250
You were up late talking to Haruko-san again.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.150
She was just tutoring me.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.860
It's rare that I get to be tutored by Haruko.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:40.800
I see.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.580
If you want to stay with Haruko-san...

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:47.240
Don't say any more!

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.040
Ren?

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:50.640
What's wrong with you?

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:53.120
I told you, I'm not going to Switzerland!

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.100
Or would you rather I go so you 
don't have to take care of me?

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:57.460
Ren...

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.380
Sorry for asking. I'm sorry.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.260
I was just a little jealous.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.760
I'm sorry for testing you.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.290
Haruko...

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:10.950
Huh?

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.270
She's just doing for me what 
she wanted to do for you.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.480
Eating together. Teaching me.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:21.960
Reading to me until I fall asleep.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.280
Staying by my side when I'm sick.

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:31.220
Mikiko said Haruko must've 
realized she was lonely

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:34.290
since she let two of her sons go.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:39.370
I want to help Haruko if I can,

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.930
but I'm just a "fake."

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.250
I'm no substitute for her real son.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:51.900
Ren, don't call yourself a fake.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.310
You and Haruko-san are a proper family.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.120
You're right.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:02.970
<i>Haru's family is more important
to him than anything.</i>

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:08.380
<i>Suddenly losing the kind 
place where he belonged</i>

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.990
<i>left a big hole inside him.</i>

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:22.060
If you really can't see me as more 
than just a brother, tell me.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.640
Okay...

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:26.440
I'd appreciate it if you told 
me sooner rather than later.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:28.170
Ren?

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.840
Goodnight.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:38.280
<i>For now, I can be the brother 
Haru wants me to be.</i>

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:40.290
<i>Probably.</i>

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.490
Hello?

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.610
He just got home. I'll put him on.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:53.880
It's Onodera-san.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:54.830
Huh?

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.810
The former landlord.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.320
Oh, the old man.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:01.180
He's recovered from his injury 
and back home now.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:03.650
He says he'll take Tanuki back.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.590
This is his leash, and this is his food bowl.

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.250
This is his dog food.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:11.710
I'll buy more for you if you run out.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.510
What a pain in the rear.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.600
Anyway, this thing's a dog 
and not a raccoon dog?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:21.310
It was pitch black when I first saw him,
so I thought he was a raccoon dog.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.550
Since his name's Tanuki, 
you can keep calling him that.

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:28.360
You're not too bothered by details, huh?

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.190
He seems to like you.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.870
Wouldn't it be better if 
you became his new owner?

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.810
I can't.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:41.010
I promised Haru that I'd only take 
care of Tanuki until you got better.

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:43.630
He's taking care of me, too.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:45.880
I don't want to cause him any more trouble.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:50.520
Well, I'd always planned to take 
care of him, so I don't mind.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:54.450
Taking him for walks as part of 
my rehab isn't a bad idea.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.840
Tanuki doesn't like walks.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:01.810
When you take him outside, 
you should carry him to the park.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.420
He really is a pain in the rear.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:06.620
Take care of Tanuki.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:09.900
Sure. Tell your brother 
to come see me sometime.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:12.680
I will.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:14.410
Tanuki...

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.210
Starting today, you're 
the old man's dog again.

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:23.040
Isn't that great? 
I hope he's really nice to you.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:24.850
Later.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.310
Onodera

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:53.840
Tanuki?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.790
You can bark?

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.800
Take him home with you.

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:02.580
Gramps...

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:07.580
Even animals as small as him 
can tell you what they want.

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:11.220
Instead of worrying about your brother,

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.590
you should tell him what you want to say.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.350
I'll be back. With yokan next time.

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.070
Make it three-colored.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:30.860
Ren!

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:34.290
Great timing. I was just about to go get you.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.820
You were at old man Onodera's place, right?

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:40.120
Haru, Tanuki doesn't...

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.570
I know.

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:46.830
It was heartless of you to try to return him 
after living with him for three months.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:50.840
I was only taking care of 
Tanuki for the old man, so...

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:56.300
Maybe at first, but Tanuki's 
part of the family now.

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:57.840
Right, Tanuki?

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.250
Does that mean we can keep him?

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:05.170
I'm always slow to notice things.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:08.450
Aki gets mad at me 
all the time for being slow.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:15.280
I was supposed to have learned my lesson 
after you ran away from me once.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:18.870
What are you talking about?

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:21.490
What you said yesterday before bed.

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:25.120
What's got you so worried?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.920
I know you're mad at me 
for treating you like a child.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:30.280
But it's only natural for 
me to worry about you.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:33.430
There are all kinds of things 
that I want to do for you.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:36.930
But you tell me you don't need them.

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:38.630
And then you said that to me yesterday.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:44.640
If you really can't see me as more 
than just a brother, tell me.

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.270
I'm amazed you could say that.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:49.610
Where have you been looking?

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:51.770
Why are you worried? 
What do you want me to do?

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:53.900
Haru!

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.580
Come with me. We shouldn't 
be discussing this outside.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.780
But Haruko's inside. And Shima.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.740
They're not home.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:03.520
Haruko-san just called to say 
she'd be late coming home.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.810
And Shima's with Aki at the Sagamis' house.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.400
There, sit.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.290
So what do you want to say to me?

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:11.990
Haru...

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.960
There are plenty of things 
you don't say to me.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:17.400
Ren.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.740
You're always in a bad mood 
when Haruko and I talk.

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:24.930
Yeah, sorry. But I apologized 
yesterday, right?

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:28.150
When you're mad, you usually ignore me.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.330
I really hate it.

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:32.490
If you're mad at me, say so.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.640
You're hard enough to read as it is.

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:37.310
It hurts me even more when 
you try to evade me with smiles.

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:39.840
Okay, I won't do it anymore. What else?

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:41.750
Ren.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:46.230
Remember when your customers from 
your previous job came to the café?

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:48.950
They kissed you. I didn't like seeing that.

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:51.360
Sorry. I won't do that anymore, either.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:55.550
And you received a photo of a girl 
from a customer the other day, right?

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:57.930
Kiyoka told me.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:00.460
She said she was a prospective bride for you.

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:01.640
Are you going to meet her?

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:03.300
No way. Absolutely not.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:03.920
And...

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:04.970
There's more?

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:12.480
R-Ren?

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.070
I'll say it again: I'm not going to Switzerland.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.980
I'll stay with you.

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:21.990
<i>Oh, jeez! This kid!</i>

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:26.990
Wha... Haru!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.590
Sorry, Ren. I can't take it anymore.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:30.960
Let me touch you.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:40.480
<i>My face feels hot.</i>

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:44.680
<i>So does my body.</i>

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:52.200
Come and have even more fun 
with your naughty brother.

00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:00.530
You're so cute, Ren.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:02.940
Don't look at me!

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:06.910
Why are you acting shy now?

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:11.350
It's kind of impressive 
that I'm doing this with you.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:15.470
You've always been small 
since you were a kid.

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:17.540
Ren?

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:21.050
Huh? What? Is something wrong?

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.280
I know I'm just a kid!

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:25.850
Don't compare me to yourself!

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:27.050
Did I step on a mine?

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.560
That's not what I meant!

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:32.330
Calm down! You're still growing!

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:33.480
You'll get bigger!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:34.430
As big as you?

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:36.430
Whoa, let's be realistic, okay?

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:44.450
<i>I was feeling excited that our loving 
relationship had taken another step forward...</i>

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:46.950
Haru, open the door!

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:49.950
Come on, I'm hungry, damn it!

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:50.970
It's Haruko!

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Ren, w-wait!

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:59.160
<i>Why do I feel like I was just 
dragged a hundred steps backward?</i>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:40.220
Next Time
